WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.201
A Brownsville, Texas,

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:02.736
man with a, quote, extensive rap sheet,

00:00:02.736 --> 00:00:03.336
including prior

00:00:03.336 --> 00:00:05.605
charges of driving while intoxicated,

00:00:05.605 --> 00:00:06.206
has been charged

00:00:06.206 --> 00:00:08.041
with eight counts of manslaughter.

00:00:08.041 --> 00:00:08.641
Authorities say

00:00:08.641 --> 00:00:10.777
that the man was driving an SUV

00:00:10.777 --> 00:00:13.046
when he ran a red light,

00:00:13.046 --> 00:00:14.114
lost control

00:00:14.114 --> 00:00:16.149
and flipped the Range Rover on its side,

00:00:16.449 --> 00:00:18.218
striking 18 people

00:00:18.218 --> 00:00:18.985
at a bus stop

00:00:18.985 --> 00:00:21.054
outside a migrant shelter and killing

00:00:21.054 --> 00:00:21.521
eight of them,

00:00:21.521 --> 00:00:23.590
most of whom were Venezuelan,

00:00:23.590 --> 00:00:24.824
according to authorities.

00:00:24.824 --> 00:00:26.593
Video obtained exclusively by CNN

00:00:26.593 --> 00:00:27.861
shows a group of people

00:00:27.861 --> 00:00:29.329
trying to restrain the man

00:00:29.329 --> 00:00:30.363
after the crash.

00:00:30.363 --> 00:00:31.031
Witnesses say

00:00:31.031 --> 00:00:32.432
he exited his vehicle

00:00:32.432 --> 00:00:34.234
and appeared to be impaired.

00:00:34.234 --> 00:00:36.536
He seemed to try to run away.

00:00:36.569 --> 00:00:39.539
He yelled obscenities, but he was stopped

00:00:40.173 --> 00:00:42.075
standing on the Texas-Mexico border.

00:00:42.075 --> 00:00:44.010
Migrants are sleeping on the streets

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:44.644
of El Paso

00:00:44.644 --> 00:00:45.278
today, a city

00:00:45.278 --> 00:00:46.379
under a state of emergency

00:00:46.379 --> 00:00:46.980
as the

00:00:47.047 --> 00:00:48.815
pandemic era public health rule

00:00:48.815 --> 00:00:50.417
that previously allowed the US government

00:00:50.417 --> 00:00:51.951
both under Trump and Biden,

00:00:51.951 --> 00:00:53.620
to turn away asylum speakers.

00:00:53.620 --> 00:00:55.588
The rule, known as Title 42,

00:00:55.588 --> 00:00:57.223
is set to expire on Thursday.

00:00:57.223 --> 00:00:58.324
It's not just El Paso,

00:00:58.324 --> 00:00:59.926
of course, facing the surge.

00:00:59.926 --> 00:01:01.294
One organization in Laredo,

00:01:01.294 --> 00:01:03.363
Texas, says that it is receiving

00:01:03.363 --> 00:01:06.332
250 migrants per day, up from 50 per day

00:01:06.332 --> 00:01:08.435
two weeks ago in McAllen, Texas.

00:01:08.468 --> 00:01:09.002
One shelter

00:01:09.002 --> 00:01:10.403
is getting 400 migrants

00:01:10.403 --> 00:01:11.037
a day,

00:01:11.037 --> 00:01:12.939
up from 152 weeks ago,

00:01:12.939 --> 00:01:14.607
and that a Brownsville, Texas, shelter.

00:01:14.607 --> 00:01:16.009
Officials say a couple of weeks ago

00:01:16.009 --> 00:01:17.911
they were seeing between 150 to 300

00:01:17.911 --> 00:01:18.611
migrants a day.

00:01:18.611 --> 00:01:20.847
Now, which 1000 a day?

00:01:20.947 --> 00:01:21.714
1000.

00:01:21.714 --> 00:01:23.616
CNN Steven Culver is in Mexico

00:01:23.616 --> 00:01:25.652
with harrowing stories of migrants

00:01:25.652 --> 00:01:26.953
on the other side of the border

00:01:28.388 --> 00:01:29.989
at the US southern border.

00:01:29.989 --> 00:01:32.058
The struggle is constant.

00:01:32.058 --> 00:01:34.094
Illegal crossings like this one

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:36.596
really tough to watch.

00:01:36.596 --> 00:01:37.764
Having already clawed

00:01:37.764 --> 00:01:39.132
through the barbed wire,

00:01:39.132 --> 00:01:40.333
you can see this young woman

00:01:40.333 --> 00:01:42.135
frustrated, exhausted,

00:01:42.135 --> 00:01:43.536
trying to help the other,

00:01:43.536 --> 00:01:45.105
trapped in a web of sharp

00:01:45.105 --> 00:01:47.574
metal at the Texas border.

00:01:47.574 --> 00:01:48.274
From above,

00:01:48.274 --> 00:01:49.075
you might think

00:01:49.075 --> 00:01:51.211
they're the only two crossing this day,

00:01:51.211 --> 00:01:53.446
but the clothes dangling along the miles

00:01:53.446 --> 00:01:55.849
and miles of fencing say otherwise.

00:01:57.450 --> 00:01:59.185
For many migrants fleeing countries

00:01:59.185 --> 00:02:00.120
like Venezuela,

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:02.188
Nicaragua, Cuba and others,

00:02:02.522 --> 00:02:04.290
Ciudad Juarez, Mexico

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:05.925
is the final stop before

00:02:05.925 --> 00:02:07.961
trying to claim asylum in the U.S..

00:02:08.061 --> 00:02:10.063
Can they wait in places like this?

00:02:10.063 --> 00:02:11.731
You can see the sidewalk.

00:02:11.731 --> 00:02:14.033
It's full of an encampment.

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:15.568
Different tents.

00:02:15.568 --> 00:02:16.870
We've seen thousands

00:02:16.870 --> 00:02:18.304
flooding the streets in shelters

00:02:18.304 --> 00:02:20.106
at this Mexican border town.

00:02:20.106 --> 00:02:21.274
22 year old Janine

00:02:21.274 --> 00:02:22.642
Gamez, her husband

00:02:22.642 --> 00:02:23.276
and their four year

00:02:23.276 --> 00:02:24.177
old little girl,

00:02:24.177 --> 00:02:25.145
have camped out here

00:02:25.145 --> 00:02:27.380
for three months already.

00:02:27.380 --> 00:02:29.182
You're got to stop it on welfare and

00:02:29.182 --> 00:02:29.782
get on with them.

00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:31.951
She says they're going to cross,

00:02:31.951 --> 00:02:33.520
but she doesn't want to do it illegally.

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:35.555
She wants to do it the right way.

00:02:36.623 --> 00:02:37.991
And does it no service.

00:02:37.991 --> 00:02:39.726
Cuando you don't know when?

00:02:39.726 --> 00:02:40.960
No secondo.

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:42.328
In recent weeks, the U.S.

00:02:42.328 --> 00:02:43.863
government has rolled out an updated

00:02:43.863 --> 00:02:45.598
CBP one app

00:02:45.598 --> 00:02:46.566
allowing migrants

00:02:46.566 --> 00:02:47.867
north of Mexico City

00:02:47.867 --> 00:02:48.768
to register

00:02:48.768 --> 00:02:50.703
digitally for a limited number

00:02:50.703 --> 00:02:52.939
of interview spots with asylum officers.

00:02:53.339 --> 00:02:54.374
No one we've talked to

00:02:54.374 --> 00:02:54.841
has been able

00:02:54.841 --> 00:02:56.643
to secure an appointment yet.

00:02:56.643 --> 00:02:59.312
Danese not sure she'll ever get one.

00:02:59.612 --> 00:03:01.214
She lost her phone in a fire

00:03:01.214 --> 00:03:02.282
a few weeks back.

00:03:02.282 --> 00:03:04.050
But she and others tell me

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:06.052
they've come too far to turn around.

00:03:06.052 --> 00:03:07.153
Her young daughter

00:03:07.153 --> 00:03:09.255
carries the marks to prove it.

00:03:09.255 --> 00:03:11.724
He kept going like era and so

00:03:13.259 --> 00:03:14.727
says she has some burns

00:03:14.727 --> 00:03:18.198
still on her face from the sun,

00:03:18.932 --> 00:03:20.200
from being on top of the train.

00:03:21.734 --> 00:03:22.235
The journey

00:03:22.235 --> 00:03:24.037
to Juarez from southern Mexico

00:03:24.037 --> 00:03:25.672
is hundreds of miles.

00:03:25.672 --> 00:03:26.706
So many ride

00:03:26.706 --> 00:03:29.842
the rails north on top of freight trains.

00:03:30.109 --> 00:03:31.211
We caught up with one

00:03:31.211 --> 00:03:33.313
just as it was arriving into Juarez.

00:03:33.813 --> 00:03:36.282
Migrants right on top here.

00:03:36.282 --> 00:03:37.483
Many of them have made the journey

00:03:37.483 --> 00:03:38.084
on this train

00:03:38.084 --> 00:03:40.119
alone for more than 8 hours.

00:03:40.119 --> 00:03:42.188
A la la la la.

00:03:42.188 --> 00:03:44.290
Though he said they were 12 hours

00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:44.991
on the train.

00:03:44.991 --> 00:03:46.826
He said it was so cold,

00:03:46.826 --> 00:03:49.629
everything felt like ice.

00:03:49.629 --> 00:03:52.232
My my life was in my mom

00:03:52.232 --> 00:03:53.766
and my enemy, hermano,

00:03:53.766 --> 00:03:55.501
his whole family here.

00:03:55.501 --> 00:03:56.936
And he says, now they are going to stay

00:03:56.936 --> 00:03:58.571
and get cleaned up

00:03:58.571 --> 00:04:00.673
and prepare to cross into the U.S.

00:04:00.707 --> 00:04:02.175
alone or something.

00:04:03.042 --> 00:04:05.311
But Leonardo's mom is terrified

00:04:05.311 --> 00:04:06.212
to climb down.

00:04:06.212 --> 00:04:08.248
I don't know where

00:04:08.681 --> 00:04:10.250
they're going to get him out or anything.

00:04:10.250 --> 00:04:12.785
Her loved ones at first encouraging,

00:04:13.186 --> 00:04:15.288
then telling her, let's go.

00:04:15.521 --> 00:04:17.557
Not that they will need by most.

00:04:17.657 --> 00:04:19.292
But part of the train

00:04:19.292 --> 00:04:20.426
journey north for some

00:04:20.426 --> 00:04:21.294
is on what's called

00:04:21.294 --> 00:04:22.228
La Bestia,

00:04:22.228 --> 00:04:24.664
the Beast or the train of Death.

00:04:25.098 --> 00:04:26.165
A ride dangerous

00:04:26.165 --> 00:04:27.433
and deadly and often

00:04:27.433 --> 00:04:29.335
controlled by cartels.

00:04:29.335 --> 00:04:29.902
Hours

00:04:29.902 --> 00:04:32.405
making this treacherous trek is scarring.

00:04:32.939 --> 00:04:35.842
But imagine days on board.

00:04:35.842 --> 00:04:38.044
And as Drinkwater is a commuter.

00:04:38.478 --> 00:04:40.847
I was very lucky, she says.

00:04:40.947 --> 00:04:42.282
They were four days on this train,

00:04:42.282 --> 00:04:42.649
she says.

00:04:42.649 --> 00:04:44.851
Horrible, really cold, he says.

00:04:44.851 --> 00:04:46.653
Four kids, his wife,

00:04:46.653 --> 00:04:48.221
four and a half days on the train.

00:04:48.221 --> 00:04:48.488
Yeah.

00:04:48.488 --> 00:04:49.055
When they ran out,

00:04:49.055 --> 00:04:51.090
I went on myself from there.

00:04:51.591 --> 00:04:53.559
I ran across to see.

00:04:53.559 --> 00:04:55.928
We see it, but I'm okay.

00:04:55.928 --> 00:04:57.063
Clive Palmer. Kazu.

00:04:57.063 --> 00:04:59.365
Mama, this is the song American.

00:04:59.565 --> 00:05:01.401
He says it's for the American dream.

00:05:01.401 --> 00:05:02.468
They're going to try to cross today

00:05:03.670 --> 00:05:04.070
another

00:05:04.070 --> 00:05:05.438
25 miles under

00:05:05.438 --> 00:05:07.540
the hot sun to the border from here.

00:05:07.540 --> 00:05:10.043
Precious cargo carried on shoulders

00:05:10.476 --> 00:05:13.880
and in hand by Venezuela.

00:05:15.014 --> 00:05:17.083
Most end up where we started

00:05:17.283 --> 00:05:18.751
at the barbed wire.

00:05:18.751 --> 00:05:19.652
The added barrier

00:05:19.652 --> 00:05:20.987
rolled out in recent months

00:05:20.987 --> 00:05:22.922
by the Texas National Guard.

00:05:22.922 --> 00:05:25.258
It does not stop the crossings.

00:05:25.258 --> 00:05:27.760
It does slow them a bit.

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:29.429
The young woman uses her jacket

00:05:29.429 --> 00:05:30.596
to create a gap

00:05:30.596 --> 00:05:32.131
while the other tosses through it

00:05:32.131 --> 00:05:34.233
bottles of water and a backpack.

00:05:34.767 --> 00:05:37.170
Their only belongings, a quick hug.

00:05:37.337 --> 00:05:38.738
And they hurry along.

00:05:38.738 --> 00:05:40.907
Likely to turn themselves in to U.S.

00:05:40.907 --> 00:05:45.445
officials, more will follow.

00:05:46.946 --> 00:05:49.148
And this is where many of them end up.

00:05:49.148 --> 00:05:50.850
You can see them camped out behind me.

00:05:50.850 --> 00:05:51.484
Not all of them.

00:05:51.484 --> 00:05:53.553
This is just a small portion

00:05:53.786 --> 00:05:54.887
of the thousands of migrants

00:05:54.887 --> 00:05:55.588
that we've seen cross

00:05:55.588 --> 00:05:57.156
over here into Ciudad Juarez,

00:05:57.156 --> 00:05:59.325
trying to cross ultimately into the U.S..

00:05:59.325 --> 00:06:00.493
Here's the thing, Jake, though.

00:06:00.493 --> 00:06:02.195
When Thursday comes

00:06:02.195 --> 00:06:05.398
and if Title 42 lifts, that by no means

00:06:05.832 --> 00:06:07.233
says that all these folks can then

00:06:07.233 --> 00:06:08.067
just go through.

00:06:08.067 --> 00:06:08.534
In fact, the U.S.

00:06:08.534 --> 00:06:10.236
is going to fall back on Title eight,

00:06:10.236 --> 00:06:11.804
which means that these folks

00:06:11.804 --> 00:06:14.073
will have their chance to claim asylum

00:06:14.374 --> 00:06:16.442
to be preliminarily screened,

00:06:16.442 --> 00:06:17.110
and for their case

00:06:17.110 --> 00:06:18.811
to be potentially heard.

00:06:18.811 --> 00:06:20.346
But under Title 42,

00:06:20.346 --> 00:06:21.047
they didn't have that.

00:06:21.047 --> 00:06:21.848
They were sent back

00:06:21.848 --> 00:06:23.583
in some cases immediately.

00:06:23.583 --> 00:06:25.618
However, if they go through that title

00:06:25.618 --> 00:06:26.853
process, Jake,

00:06:26.853 --> 00:06:28.121
and their cases fail

00:06:28.121 --> 00:06:28.588
and they don't

00:06:28.588 --> 00:06:30.123
have enough to prove asylum,

00:06:30.123 --> 00:06:31.557
they can be banned from the U.S.

00:06:31.557 --> 00:06:33.092
for some five years.

00:06:33.092 --> 00:06:35.495
So in many cases, it's

00:06:35.495 --> 00:06:36.829
the stakes are much higher

00:06:36.829 --> 00:06:39.198
if they try to cross after Thursday.

00:06:39.198 --> 00:06:39.432
All right,

00:06:39.432 --> 00:06:41.267
David Culver in Mexico for us, thank

00:06:41.267 --> 00:06:41.934
you so much for.

